          body: `Both the NHS and the AAP say to brush at least twice a day; the NHS says one of the brushes should be before bed, and the AAP suggests typically after breakfast and before bed.\n\nChildren cannot brush well on their own for years. The NHS says to keep helping until your child can do it well alone, usually until at least age 7, and the AAP says kids usually need help until about age 8 and should still be supervised afterwards. Netzwerk Gesund ins Leben adds that adults should put the toothpaste on the brush so the amount is right.\n\nIf your baby protests, you do not have to win the fight. The German Netzwerk Gesund ins Leben advises never brushing against the child's resistance: try again at the next opportunity, and songs or stories can help.`,
